=== gimp
--- gimp --s
--session=	use an alternate sessionrc file (sessionrc.NAME)
--show-playground 	show a preferences page with experimental features
--stack-trace-mode=	debug in case of a crash
--system-gimprc=	use an alternate system gimprc file
--- gimp -
--batch-interpreter=	the procedure to run batch commands with
--debug-handlers 	enable non-fatal debugging signal handlers
--display=	the X display to use
--dump-gimprc 	print a gimprc file with the default settings
--g-fatal-warnings 	make all warnings fatal
--gegl-cache-size=	how much memory to use for caching imagery
--gegl-chunk-size=	the number of pixels to compute at once
--gegl-disable-opencl 	disable OpenCL
--gegl-quality=	the quality of rendering (0.0 fast to 1.0 reference)
--gegl-swap-compression=	compression of the data in the swap
--gegl-swap=	where GEGL stores its swap
--gegl-threads=	the number of processing threads
--gegl-tile-size=	default size of tiles in GeglBuffers
--help-all 	show all the help
--help-gegl 	show GEGL's options
--help-gtk 	show GTK's options
--license 	show the license
--no-cpu-accel 	don't use special CPU acceleration functions
--no-shm 	don't use shared memory between GIMP and plug-ins
--pdb-compat-mode=	PDB compatibility mode
--quit 	quit after performing the requested actions
--session=	use an alternate sessionrc file (sessionrc.NAME)
--show-playground 	show a preferences page with experimental features
--stack-trace-mode=	debug in case of a crash
--system-gimprc=	use an alternate system gimprc file
--verbose 	be more verbose
-a 	open images as new
-b 	batch command to run (- for standard input)
-c 	send messages to the console instead of a dialog
-d 	don't load brushes, gradients, patterns, ...
-f 	don't load any fonts
-g 	use an alternate user gimprc file
-h 	show the help
-i 	run without a user interface
-n 	start a new GIMP
-s 	don't show a splash screen
-v 	show the version
